(LIB-30 -- LANGUAGE.md:5013-5016 claims a repeat --shared build will not
 overwrite an existing .lib: it should error and ask you to remove the
 .lib first. It does not; this is Discrepancy 1, and D1.vox is its
 minimal repro. This file is the fuller version: it also shows a
 hand-edited .lib line surviving as far as the *first* rebuild's read,
 then getting silently overwritten by the *second*.
 Ran, from the repo root, in a scratch directory:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm
   V=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox
   $V docs/ledger/probes/libraries/shared/LIB-overwrite.vox --shared -o overwrite.so
   echo "PINNED EDIT" >> overwrite.lib
   $V docs/ledger/probes/libraries/shared/LIB-overwrite.vox --shared -o overwrite.so
   cat overwrite.lib
 expected output: both builds exit 0 with no diagnostic, and the final
 overwrite.lib does NOT contain the "PINNED EDIT" line -- it was silently
 replaced with a freshly generated .lib:
   Library mathkit version "1.0".
   Location "./overwrite.so".

   Table of Contents:
       To 'add two numbers' with a number called x and a number called y, returning a number.
       To greet.
)

Library mathkit version "1.0".

To 'add two numbers' with a number called x and a number called y. Return a number, x add y.

To greet.
  Print "hello from mathkit".
